        "# WordPress Development Best Practices for cFish.io\r",
        "\r",
        "This document outlines the recommended best practices for developing and maintaining the cFish.io WordPress site.\r",
        "\r",
        "## Coding Standards\r",
        "\r",
        "### PHP\r",
        "\r",
        "- Follow [WordPress PHP Coding Standards](https://developer.wordpress.org/coding-standards/wordpress-coding-standards/php/)\r",
        "- Use PHP 7.4+ compatible code\r",
        "- Properly sanitize inputs and escape outputs\r",
        "- Use meaningful variable and function names\r",
        "- Add comments for complex logic\r",
        "- Use proper indentation (4 spaces)\r",
        "\r",
        "### CSS\r",
        "\r",
        "- Follow [WordPress CSS Coding Standards](https://developer.wordpress.org/coding-standards/wordpress-coding-standards/css/)\r",
        "- Use descriptive class names\r",
        "- Organize CSS with logical grouping\r",
        "- Minimize use of !important declarations\r",
        "- Use CSS preprocessors (SASS/LESS) when beneficial\r",
        "- Follow mobile-first approach for responsive design\r",
        "\r",
        "### JavaScript\r",
        "\r",
        "- Follow [WordPress JavaScript Coding Standards](https://developer.wordpress.org/coding-standards/wordpress-coding-standards/javascript/)\r",
        "- Use modern ES6+ syntax where browser support allows\r",
        "- Properly enqueue scripts in WordPress\r",
        "- Add useful comments for complex logic\r",
        "- Minimize jQuery usage when vanilla JS is sufficient\r",
        "- Always consider performance implications\r",
        "\r",
        "## WordPress-Specific Practices\r",
        "\r",
        "### Theme Development\r",
        "\r",
        "- Use child themes for customizations when appropriate\r",
        "- Implement proper template hierarchy\r",
        "- Keep template files focused on presentation logic\r",
        "- Utilize WordPress template tags appropriately\r",
        "- Follow WordPress accessibility guidelines\r",
        "- Implement proper translation/internationalization\r",
        "\r",
        "### Plugin Usage\r",
        "\r",
        "- Only use necessary plugins\r",
        "- Favor well-maintained, frequently updated plugins\r",
        "- Check plugin compatibility before updates\r",
        "- Avoid plugins that significantly impact performance\r",
        "- Document custom plugin configurations\r",
        "\r",
        "### Custom Functionality\r",
        "\r",
        "- Use custom post types for specialized content\r",
        "- Implement custom taxonomies when appropriate\r",
        "- Create focused single-purpose functions\r",
        "- Leverage WordPress hooks (actions/filters) properly\r",
        "- Follow WordPress database schema conventions\r",
        "- Avoid direct database queries when possible\r",
        "\r",
        "## Security Practices\r",
        "\r",
        "### Code Security\r",
        "\r",
        "- Validate and sanitize all user inputs\r",
        "- Escape data before output\r",
        "- Use prepared SQL statements\r",
        "- Implement proper capability checks\r",
        "- Follow principle of least privilege\r",
        "- Keep WordPress core, themes, and plugins updated\r",
        "\r",
        "### Authentication & Authorization\r",
        "\r",
        "- Use strong passwords\r",
        "- Implement two-factor authentication where possible\r",
        "- Limit login attempts\r",
        "- Regularly audit user accounts and permissions\r",
        "- Remove unnecessary user roles\r",
        "\r",
        "### File & Server Security\r",
        "\r",
        "- Protect sensitive files (.htaccess, wp-config.php)\r",
        "- Use HTTPS for all traffic\r",
        "- Implement proper file permissions\r",
        "- Set up security headers\r",
        "- Consider using a Web Application Firewall\r",
        "\r",
        "## Performance Optimization\r",
        "\r",
        "### Code Optimization\r",
        "\r",
        "- Minimize database queries\r",
        "- Use transients API for caching\r",
        "- Optimize functions.php\r",
        "- Defer JavaScript loading when possible\r",
        "- Avoid unnecessary code execution\r",
        "\r",
        "### Asset Optimization\r",
        "\r",
        "- Minimize and combine CSS/JS files\r",
        "- Optimize image files (compression, proper dimensions)\r",
        "- Use modern image formats (WebP when possible)\r",
        "- Implement lazy loading for images and videos\r",
        "- Use proper image srcset for responsive images\r",
        "\r",
        "### WordPress Optimization\r",
        "\r",
        "- Use a caching plugin\r",
        "- Optimize database regularly\r",
        "- Limit post revisions\r",
        "- Disable unused features\r",
        "- Consider a CDN for static assets\r",
        "\r",
        "## Version Control Practices\r",
        "\r",
        "### Branching Strategy\r",
        "\r",
        "- Use feature branches for all changes\r",
        "- Name branches descriptively (feature/, bugfix/, hotfix/)\r",
        "- Keep branches small and focused\r",
        "- Regularly sync with main branch\r",
        "- Delete branches after merging\r",
        "\r",
        "### Commit Practices\r",
        "\r",
        "- Write clear, descriptive commit messages\r",
        "- Make small, focused commits\r",
        "- Reference issue numbers when applicable\r",
        "- Group related changes in a single commit\r",
        "- Commit often to preserve history\r",
        "\r",
        "### Code Review\r",
        "\r",
        "- All changes should be reviewed before merging\r",
        "- Use pull requests for significant changes\r",
        "- Verify functionality before approving\r",
        "- Check for coding standards compliance\r",
        "- Document review process and findings\r",
        "\r",
        "## Testing Practices\r",
        "\r",
        "### Manual Testing\r",
        "\r",
        "- Test on multiple browsers and devices\r",
        "- Check all user flows\r",
        "- Verify responsive behavior\r",
        "- Test with different user roles\r",
        "- Validate accessibility\r",
        "\r",
        "### Automated Testing (if implemented)\r",
        "\r",
        "- Write unit tests for custom functions\r",
        "- Implement integration tests for critical flows\r",
        "- Set up visual regression testing\r",
        "- Run tests before deploying\r",
        "- Maintain test documentation\r",
        "\r",
        "## Documentation\r",
        "\r",
        "### Code Documentation\r",
        "\r",
        "- Document functions with PHPDoc comments\r",
        "- Explain complex logic\r",
        "- Document custom hooks\r",
        "- Include parameter and return value descriptions\r",
        "- Note any dependencies or side effects\r",
        "\r",
        "### Project Documentation\r",
        "\r",
        "- Maintain up-to-date README\r",
        "- Document environment setup\r",
        "- Keep track of configuration changes\r",
        "- Document custom features\r",
        "- Create user guides when needed\r",
        "\r",
        "## Collaboration\r",
        "\r",
        "### Communication\r",
        "\r",
        "- Document decisions and rationale\r",
        "- Use clear language in all communications\r",
        "- Provide context when discussing changes\r",
        "- Ask questions when requirements are unclear\r",
        "- Share knowledge with team members\r",
        "\r",
        "### Workflow\r",
        "\r",
        "- Follow established SOPs\r",
        "- Use issue tracking for tasks\r",
        "- Keep project management tools updated\r",
        "- Schedule regular reviews\r",
        "- Document lessons learned\r",
        "\r",
        "## WordPress.com Specific\r",
        "\r",
        "### Platform Limitations\r",
        "\r",
        "- Be aware of WordPress.com restrictions\r",
        "- Understand differences between WordPress.com and self-hosted\r",
        "- Follow WordPress.com specific guidelines\r",
        "- Test platform-specific features\r",
        "- Document WordPress.com specific configurations\r",
        "\r",
        "### Deployment Considerations\r",
        "\r",
        "- Follow proper backup procedures\r",
        "- Test extensively before deploying\r",
        "- Use consistent deployment process\r",
        "- Document deployment steps\r",
        "- Plan for rollback if needed"
      ]
    }
  ],
